lesson: 202
title: Legs on four-legged animals
level: primary-3
stars: 0
explain: Dogs, cats, mice, lions, giraffes, horses, tortoises and lizards each walk on 4 legs.
explain: When all the animals have 4 legs, add the animals first and then multiply by 4.
explain: 2 giraffes and 3 lions are 5 animals, so they have 5 × 4 = 20 legs.
vars: a=name b=name x=2..9 y=2..9
answer: 4 * (x + y)
exercise: At the zoo there are {x} giraffes and {y} lions. How many legs do they have altogether?
exercise: {a} has {x} dogs and {y} cats on the farm. How many legs do the pets have?
exercise: In the barn live {x} mice and {y} cats. How many legs is that in all?
exercise: The pet shop has {x} tortoises and {y} lizards. How many legs do they have together?
exercise: A carousel has {x} wooden horses and {y} wooden lions. How many wooden legs does it have?
exercise: {a} walks {x} dogs and {b} walks {y} dogs. How many dog legs are in the park?
exercise: zoo trip! {x} giraffes and {y} lions, how many legs
exercise: we got {x} cats n {y} dogs at nan's, total legs?
exercise: {x} lizards and {y} tortoises at the pet shop, the guy said the tortoise is like 80 yrs old. legs altogether?
exercise: {a} has {y+1} mice — sorry, {y} mice — and {x} cats, which is a bad idea. how many legs
exercise: my mate says {x} dogs and {y} cats got {x+y} legs cos one each lol. how many really
test: Count the legs of {y} lions and {x} giraffes.
test: What is the total number of legs on {x} horses and {y} dogs standing in a field?
test: {b} counts the animals at the farm show: {x} cats and {y} dogs. How many legs did {b.he} count?
test: {y} mice run under the floor, and {x} cats sit waiting by the hole. How many legs is that?
test: Find the number of legs on a carousel with {x} wooden horses and {y} wooden giraffes.
test: {x} dogs + {y} cats on the sofa. legs?
test: legs on {x} giraffes and {y} lions, the lions were asleep btw
exam: Determine the aggregate number of legs belonging to {x.words} giraffes and {y.words} lions held in a zoological collection.
exam: It is given that a household maintains {x} dogs and {y} cats. Ascertain the total quantity of legs pertaining to these animals.
exam: A carousel is furnished with {x} wooden horses and {y} wooden lions, each carved in the likeness of the living animal. Compute the total number of legs so carved.
exam: Whereas a pet shop holds {x} tortoises and {y} lizards, state the combined number of legs thereof.
exercise: The farm had {x+1} dogs and {y} cats, but the oldest dog was put to sleep last week. How many legs do the pets have now?
exercise: When Gran moved into assisted living, {a} took in her {x} cats and {y} rabbits. How many legs do these pets have?
test: {b}'s mum got let go so they rehomed their pets with us lol. now we got {x} dogs n {y} cats in total. legs? stop screaming
